    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d839">

                <pb facs="0962" n="818" xml:id="pg818"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/5113: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-02-07T19:00:00-05:00">February 7, 1929—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>54. Your 59, January 28, 3 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Have you acted on the Department’s telegram 414 of December 19, 3
                            p.m.,<anchor n="75" xml:id="d839-f1"/> and if so with what
                        result?</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Department wishes to avoid any commitment on its part regarding Wang’s
                        note of January 18, and proposal in your paragraph 2 is approved as
                        satisfactory in this regard.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
